From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:08:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 107/128] render: an HDR scene's image brightness scales its
 draw colour, as WE's
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wallpaper Engine sets an image's draw-context colour (g_Color, g_Color4.rgb) to the layer's colour times its
`brightness` when the renderer runs HDR (flag 0x2000: post-processing Ultra with a scene whose general has
`bloom` and `hdr`), and times 1 otherwise (GH 0x1402321d0, 0x1402328e0, 0x140231dc0: ctx+0x124…0x12c =
image+0x330…0x338 × (ctx flags & 0x2000 ? image+0x340 : 1)). The VERSION image shaders and genericimage4
have no g_Brightness term, so this is the only place such a layer's brightness shows. LWE never applied it:
2542468435's single layer (genericimage2 VERSION 2, brightness 1.15) drew 15 % too dark, and its values
above 1 never reached the HDR bloom (gap audit E42). g_Brightness is unchanged.

The WE reference of 2542468435 (re-encoded from WE's FP16 swap chain) scores 0.481 -> 0.022.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-proton.md "The FP16 swap chain"; gap audit E42 (2542468435)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.h   |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index f781665..74b54c3 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -1784,7 +1784,15 @@ const float& CImage::getUserAlpha () const { return this->m_image.alpha->value->
 
 const float& CImage::getAlpha () const { return this->m_image.alpha->value->getFloat (); }
 
-const glm::vec3& CImage::getColor () const { return this->m_image.color->value->getVec3 (); }
+const glm::vec3& CImage::getColor () const {
+    // WE's draw context colour (g_Color, g_Color4.rgb) is the layer's colour × its brightness when the renderer runs
+    // HDR (flag 0x2000), else × 1 (GH 0x1402321d0 / 0x1402328e0 / 0x140231dc0: ctx+0x124…0x12c = image+0x330…0x338 ×
+    // (ctx flags & 0x2000 ? image+0x340 : 1)). The VERSION shaders have no g_Brightness term, so this is where an HDR
+    // scene's `brightness` shows (2542468435's 1.15). Bound by address: refreshed by getColor4 () every render ()
+    const float brightness = this->getScene ().rendersHDR () ? this->getBrightness () : 1.0f;
+    this->m_drawColor = this->m_image.color->value->getVec3 () * brightness;
+    return this->m_drawColor;
+}
 
 const glm::vec4& CImage::getColor4 () const {
     // WE's g_Color4 is (g_Color, g_Alpha): the colour and the layer's alpha, not the colour value's own w
diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.h b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.h
index deff9dc..8e9fbc4 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.h
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.h
@@ -345,6 +345,8 @@ private:
     bool m_initialized = false;
     /** (color.rgb, alpha) for g_Color4, refreshed by getColor4 () — every render () */
     mutable glm::vec4 m_color4 = glm::vec4 (1.0f);
+    /** g_Color: the colour, × brightness in an HDR scene (GH 0x1402321d0), refreshed by getColor4 () */
+    mutable glm::vec3 m_drawColor = glm::vec3 (1.0f);
 
